 ### [Image-based reconstruction optimization](6677-image-based-reconstruction-optimization.md)
-Image-based reconstruction optimization solves for object shapes, poses, textures, and lighting by minimizing image losses using gradients estimated via differentiable rendering pipelines. It sets itself apart from its siblings by explicitly formulating the inverse problem as an unconstrained optimization task where latent parameters (such as shape vectors and pose angles) are updated via gradient descent to minimize the photometric difference between a rendered image and an observed target. Unlike [Gradient-Based SE(3) Optimization](7526-gradient-based-se-3-optimization.md), which may focus on rigid body transformations, this approach often jointly optimizes complex latent shape representations and appearance parameters.
